VB-MAPP is an evidenced based assessment commonly used for early learners with language delays and autism spectrum disorder.<br><br><strong>Booeys: Rip in the Rift</strong> seamlessly integrates with your curriculum, aligning with educational standards and VB-MAPP goals for visual perception and matching skills. Students sort objects based on various criteria, mirroring activities you already use in the classroom. This game effectively supports:<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Early learners: Identify identical objects (fruits, shapes) like Kindergarten standards.<br></li><li>Developing learners: Group similar items (colors, categories) like Grade 1-2 expectations.<br></li><li>Advanced students: Find variations within categories (textures, patterns) like Grade 3 and above challenges.</li></ul><br>Booeys engages the player with embedded visual prompts subtly guiding players, mimicking therapist instructions, and \u201cexplosive\u201d scenes when matching correctly. As children play, Booeys tracks their progress. See accuracy rates, submitted items, and active input time, gaining valuable insights into their development. This data can be shared with clinicians, educators, and parents to guide further learning and interventions.",
